# One feature per branch

A branch ships one reviewable change. Do not mix unrelated features, refactors, or chores.

## Split like this

- `chore/bootstrap`: ignore, env example, dependencies, run docs
- `feat/chat-search`: agent loop, search tool, chat API
- `feat/voice-input`: transcription API and talk button
- `feat/desktop-shell`: desktop window only

Voice, search, and the desktop wrapper are three branches, not one.

## Do

- Name branches `feat/`, `fix/`, or `chore/` plus a short scope
- Stack only when the later branch cannot compile without the earlier one
- Stage named files; never dump the whole tree into one commit
- Keep the working tree on the branch that matches the current task

## Do not

- Land an "MVP everything" commit on `main`
- Put search, voice, and desktop in the same PR
- Change git `user.name` / `user.email`
- Add Cursor as author, committer, or `Co-authored-by`
